window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["00"]={"https://theconversation.com/pasifika-women-are-making-rugby-league-history-but-what-about-the-next-generation-295741":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"cfa2cf6e87d57aee27e082d1728625785b679a64e307a5f7cb33afdff2572f1a","read":"https://theconversation.com/pasifika-women-are-making-rugby-league-history-but-what-about-the-next-generation-295741","bytes":182964,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pasifika women are making rugby league history. But what about the next generation?","by":[{"n":"Sierra Keung","r":"Lecturer in Sport and Recreation, Auckland University of Technology"},{"n":"Mihi Joy Nemani","r":"Senior Lecturer, Te Huataki Waiora School of Health, University of Waikato"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T18:21:47Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For ",["Fetu Samoa","https://samoaglobalnews.com/1history-made-fetu-samoa-qualify-for-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-finals-for-first-time/"]," and ",["Fiji Bulikula","https://fijisun.com.fj/sports/rugby/bulikula-eye-jillaroos-upset-after-making-history-at-rlwc"],", the ",["2026 Women’s Rugby League World Cup","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Women%27s_Rugby_League_World_Cup"]," marked a historic breakthrough, with both nations reaching the semifinals for the first time."]},{"k":"p","s":["While each team came up short against ",["New Zealand’s Kiwi Ferns","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/sport/rugby-league/kiwi-ferns-v-fetu-samoa-live-updates-womens-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-final/CQMWMYQFNVBYDKXAZKPJL3E6PY/"]," and ",["Australia’s Jillaroos","https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/08/australia-jillaroos-fiji-womens-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-final-match-report"]," respectively last weekend, their strong showing throughout the tournament highlighted ",["the depth of Pasifika talent in the code","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/pacific/1793479/pacific-women-s-squads-packed-with-nrl-experience-for-rugby-league-world-cup"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interestingly, players of Pacific heritage featured across all four semifinal teams, reflecting the pathways that have enabled Pasifika women to compete at the highest level."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many players representing Pacific nations have advanced through development systems in Australia and New Zealand. However, opportunities within Pacific countries themselves remain much more limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["So what pathways are needed to ensure the next generation of Pasifika players can thrive closer to home?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Paths to the top"]},{"k":"p","s":["Building better pathways means more than identifying top talent. Girls need opportunities to enter the game and keep playing. This starts with local clubs, coaching, facilities and regular competitions providing a foundation for those hoping to reach elite levels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Currently, the routes players take to international rugby league vary considerably. Fiji’s world cup squad has just one locally based player, while Samoa’s team draws heavily on talent developed through ",["Australia’s National Rugby League Women’s Premiership","https://www.nrl.com/nrlw/"]," (NRLW) system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, Papua New Guinea’s Orchids include both Australian-based players and those who have advanced through domestic clubs and competitions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But where players are based only tells part of the story. It reveals little about where they first played, who supported their development, or the connections they maintain with Pasifika communities."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research with Pasifika men","https://www.jstor.org/stable/24809728"]," in Australian rugby league highlights the importance of migration, family, faith, culture and national allegiance in their experiences of the sport. While women’s experiences differ, the findings suggest pathways into international rugby league are rarely straightforward, or confined to a single country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Keeping women in the game"]},{"k":"p","s":["The need to boost opportunities within Pacific nations comes ",["as the Australian government commits","https://www.pm.gov.au/media/scoring-tries-and-strengthening-ties-pacific"]," A$250 million over ten years to the Pacific Rugby League Partnership with Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Tonga and Fiji. Plans include girls’ and national competitions, development pathways and academies, alongside education, leadership and employment opportunities."]},{"k":"p","s":["But how much of that investment will reach women and girls? And will Pasifika women have a meaningful say in how these programmes are designed and delivered? Much will depend on how the funding is allocated and what support is available on the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research offers some insights into what makes sporting opportunities accessible."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["netball-for-development programme","https://www.academia.edu/95772657/Schulenkorf_N_Sherry_E_Siefken_K_Tauhalaliku_U_and_Richards_J_2022_Health_Interventions_as_Vehicles_for_Increased_Sport_Participation_for_Girls_and_Women_Socio_Managerial_Insights_from_a_Netball_for_Development_Program_in_Tonga_Journal_of_Sport_for_Development_10_1_25_39"]," in Tonga highlights the importance of family and community support, access to facilities and equipment, regular competitions and the volunteers who keep local sport running."]},{"k":"p","s":["More ",["recent research in Fiji","https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/sports-and-active-living/articles/10.3389/fspor.2026.1855393/full"]," found that while sport can open doors for young people, young women face particular barriers, including domestic responsibilities, financial pressures and gender expectations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Practical support for women’s health is also important. A ",["study","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/10126902251351181"]," involving Pacific sportswomen found that cultural expectations and family attitudes influence how menstruation is understood and discussed, as well as the information and support available to women in sporting environments."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings highlight the need for investment beyond elite competitions and academies. Without accessible facilities, regular opportunities to play and support that responds to women’s circumstances, even well-funded development programmes risk leaving many girls behind."]},{"k":"h","s":["Making the next play"]},{"k":"p","s":["The knowledge, relationships and experience women gain through playing can open doors to coaching, officiating, administration and leadership."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jillaroos head coach ",["Jess Skinner","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-11/jillaroos-coach-jessica-skinner-2026-rugby-league-world-cup/107098594"]," has followed such a path. A Barkindji and Māori woman, she progressed from grassroots women’s rugby league in regional New South Wales to leading Australia’s national team. Along the way, she relied on family sacrifices, community support and mentors who helped her advance. She is also the only female head coach at this world cup."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Pasifika women, opportunities to lead ",["are closely connected","https://indd.adobe.com/view/786559fb-d4b9-4548-a183-45e4ac830ef8"]," to culture, family, faith and community."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet mainstream leadership models do not always recognise Pacific approaches, potentially overlooking women with valuable knowledge and experience. More culturally grounded development programmes would help bring these women into coaching, administration and decision-making roles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women should not have to choose between pursuing professional opportunities overseas and contributing to the game at home. They should be able to do both. This builds stronger connections between domestic and international competitions allowing skills, experience and expertise to benefit rugby league across the Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["Success, then, shouldn’t be measured solely by the number of Pasifika women reaching the NRLW or international competition. It should also be evident in stronger local competitions, more women in coaching and leadership roles, and greater opportunities for the next generation to enter and remain in the game."]},{"k":"p","s":["Samoa and Fiji’s historic World Cup campaigns have shown what Pasifika women can achieve. The task now is to ensure that success translates into lasting opportunities for those who follow."]}],"chars":5503},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"ebf23e290ad96709f34521867e7f16c936597561e498e1fa42231f80c1ee37bf","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/croatia","bytes":72125,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Croatia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:43+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia/email-signup"]," for Croatia when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Croatia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Croatian Embassy in the UK","https://mvep.gov.hr/uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Croatia follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Croatia, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-croatia-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Croatian border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Croatian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Croatian Embassy in the UK","https://mvep.gov.hr/consular-information-107317/general-visa-information-107319/107319"],". See the Croatian Ministry of the Interior’s guidance on ",["work permits","https://mup.gov.hr/radne-dozvole/286764"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Croatia with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-croatia#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Croatia-Slovenia border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are checks at Slovenia’s borders with Croatia. If you are travelling from Croatia to Slovenia, check ",["travel advice for Slovenia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/slovenia/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Croatia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your accommodation provider must register your arrival in Croatia with the police within 48 hours. Your hotel will normally register you. If your accommodation provider is unable to do this for you, ",["fill in and print form obrazac 16a (PDF)","https://mup.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/stranci/2022/Obrazac-prijave-i-odjave-smjestaja-boravista-i-prebivalista-za-drz-trecih-zemalja-(Obrazac-16a).pdf"],". You must hand in the completed form at a police station. Alternatively, you should go to the nearest police station with the owner of the accommodation to register your address in Croatia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Croatia","https://carina.gov.hr/featured/information-for-passengers-natural-persons/relief-from-duties-and-restrictions/6715"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the ",["value is 10,000 euros or more","https://carina.gov.hr/featured/information-for-passengers-natural-persons/bringing-cash-and-goods-across-the-border/6711"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Croatia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low and violent crime is rare."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists have been overcharged at certain ‘gentlemen’s clubs’, sometimes by thousands of euros, and threatened with violence if they refuse to pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets operate in tourist areas. Avoid carrying large sums of cash, do not leave valuables unattended and use hotel safes if possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Attacks and sexual assaults in taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of sexual assaults in taxis in Croatia. To reduce risk and help prevent potential assaults:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a photo of the inside, where the number of the taxi is visible, and send it to a friend or someone else"]},{"k":"li","s":["share your ride status on the taxi app"]},{"k":"li","s":["make a call while in the taxi telling someone which taxi it is and where you are going"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Large gatherings, including football matches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large gatherings and public events are overwhelmingly safe and peaceful in Croatia, including sporting events. However, there are periodic cases of violence between football fans around matches. Care should be taken near football stadiums around match times, especially “derby” matches, and you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large crowds"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local news reports"]},{"k":"li","s":["comply with instructions from police"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you feel uncomfortable, leave the area immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport or, if you’re a resident, your Croatian ID card. Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Antisocial behaviour"]},{"k":"p","s":["In some Croatian town centres, including tourist destinations like Split and Dubrovnik, you can get on-the-spot fines for behaviour seen as inappropriate, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["drinking alcohol or using drugs in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["sleeping in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["urinating or vomiting in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["walking through towns shirtless or in swimwear"]},{"k":"li","s":["wearing clothing that promotes drug use"]},{"k":"li","s":["climbing on monuments"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also be fined up to 4,000 euros for public order disturbances, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["fighting"]},{"k":"li","s":["verbal abuse such as shouting or arguing"]},{"k":"li","s":["drunken behaviour"]},{"k":"li","s":["belittling or insulting police officers or other public officials"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. Carrying cannabis for personal use has been decriminalised but if found on you or in your apartment, you will be asked to pay sometimes heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Croatia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unexploded mines"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel outside the tourist resorts, beware of unexploded mines in previously war-affected areas, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eastern Slavonia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Brod-Posavina County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karlovac County"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas around Zadar County"]},{"k":"li","s":["more remote areas of the Plitvice Lakes National Park"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information about mine-affected areas, visit the ",["Civil Protection website","https://civilna-zastita.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/145"]," (in Croatian) or contact the Civil Protection offices."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling in these areas, do not walk on uncultivated land or step off the marked paths. If in doubt, get local advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiking in the mountains, get expert advice from local guides, however tame the mountain might seem. Weather in the Croatian mountains can change quickly, even in summer. Temperatures can get very low overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of getting lost in the mountains when out hiking alone and using unmarked paths. Read the ",["Croatian Mountain Rescue tips on mountaineering","https://www.hgss.hr/en/"],", follow their X at ",["Hrvatska GSS","https://x.com/hrvatskaGSS"]," and see their maps. If you get into trouble, call the emergency number 112 for help from the Croatian Mountain Rescue Service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Music festivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many music festivals are held in Croatia each year. Follow the advice of police and local authorities when attending events and take care of your valuables if attending a festival or large concert. Find out how to enjoy festivals safely with the ",["festival travel checklist","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Croatia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in RAC’s Croatia guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/croatia/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["having your headlights on and dipped when driving a car from 1 November until 31 March, even during daytime"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving with dipped headlights year-round on scooters and motorcycles"]},{"k":"li","s":["using winter tyres between 15 November and 15 April"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying a fluorescent vest in the car, not in the boot – you must wear the vest while attending to a breakdown"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Croatia for up to one year. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Croatia, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Croatian Automobile Association lists ",["current traffic hazards","https://www.hak.hr/en#traffic-flow-and-road-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Croatia. If you’re found with more than 0.05% of alcohol in your blood (in England it’s 0.08%) you will get a fine, and you may lose your licence and get a prison sentence. The alcohol limit is zero for drivers under the age of 24."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not drink alcohol if you’re in charge of a yacht or boat. There are heavy penalties for being caught drunk in charge of a boat and a zero-tolerance approach."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must sail by the most direct route to a port of entry when entering Croatian territorial waters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Authorities can arrest you for entering a non-designated entry port without telling them. If you cannot use the correct entry port, contact the local harbour master or the police before entering Croatia."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Croatia, including on a boat, your presence in Croatia must be registered with the police. If you’re travelling with a tour operator, they should do this for you. Otherwise, you must ",["fill in and print form obrazac 16a (PDF)","https://mup.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/stranci/2022/Obrazac-prijave-i-odjave-smjestaja-boravista-i-prebivalista-za-drz-trecih-zemalja-(Obrazac-16a).pdf"]," and hand it in at a police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["All captains must have an ",["International Certificate of Competence","https://www.rya.org.uk/knowledge/abroad/icc"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],". Please follow advice from local authorities and monitor ",["Croatian Meteorological and Hydrological Service","https://meteo.hr/index_en.php"]," forecasts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are common during Croatia’s hot and dry summers. They can be highly dangerous and unpredictable. The situation can change quickly. Take care when visiting or driving through woodland and forest areas. If you see a fire, call the emergency services on 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you are in or near an area affected by wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities and emergency services"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Croatian emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"li","s":["for further information, see Croatia’s ",["Civil Protection website","https://civilna-zastita.gov.hr/en"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Intentionally causing a fire is illegal in Croatia and you could be fined 2,000 to 20,000 euros, or even given a prison sentence. You could also be fined for unintentionally causing a fire. To avoid starting wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave no litter, especially not glass which is known to start fires"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not light barbecues. From 1 June to 31 October it is illegal to set outdoor fires and barbecues except in designated areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["properly extinguish cigarette ends and do not leave any rubbish behind, particularly empty bottles, as these are known to start fires"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes in Croatia can be strong and cause deaths and damage to infrastructure. In recent years, there have been earthquakes in Zagreb and in Petrinja, near Sisak in central Croatia. Both caused extensive damage to buildings and infrastructure and loss of life. Heavily damaged buildings, which are not always signposted, may be unstable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Small tremors also happen several times a month throughout the year. Most pass without consequence. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Floods"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods can happen with very little warning and lead to dangerous water flows and disruption to transport and other networks. There is the highest risk of flooding in central Croatia, between Karlovac and Slavonski Brod. Monitor ",["Croatian Meteorological and Hydrological Service","https://meteo.hr/index_en.php"]," forecasts, as well as traffic conditions with the Croatian Automobile authority and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Croatia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Croatia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-facilities-in-croatia"],", where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Croatia, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. In Croatia there is always a charge for treatment, which can be up to 530 euros. You may have other costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-croatia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travel-and-mental-health"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you’re involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Croatia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Croatia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Croatia"]," in Croatia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with ",["a death in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/croatia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/croatia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/croatia/british-embassy-zagreb"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-croatia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20381,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/jd-vance-singled-out-iran-war-for-midterm-rout-he-didnt-say-what-should-happen-next-in-conflict-295938":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"293b6d6cf87508fbadbaeb857cb8bdb094c7828cbfd777bed21ad98abf239008","read":"https://theconversation.com/jd-vance-singled-out-iran-war-for-midterm-rout-he-didnt-say-what-should-happen-next-in-conflict-295938","bytes":188368,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"JD Vance singled out Iran War for midterm rout – he didn’t say what should happen next in conflict","by":[{"n":"Javed Ali","r":"Associate Professor of Practice of Public Policy, University of Michigan"}],"pub":"2026-11-06T00:31:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["While votes were still being counted ",["in the U.S. midterm elections","https://theconversation.com/epic-blue-wave-helps-democrats-take-congress-in-overwhelming-rebuke-to-president-trump-295830"],", administration figures in Washington were already inviting speculation over how the results might be ",["connected to the conflict with Iran","https://theconversation.com/with-control-of-congress-heres-how-democrats-could-stop-trumps-war-in-iran-295954"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the morning after the election, Vice President JD Vance ",["wrote on X","https://x.com/JDVance/status/2118004988433641835"]," that the major reason for the dramatic loss for Republicans was the American public’s opposition to the war. “Everyone knows why we lost. And any honest conversation about where we go from here must start there,” he wrote, in reference to the ongoing conflict that began with U.S.-Israeli airstrikes against Iran in late February 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["While it is rare for a vice president to make such a critical proclamation about their own administration’s policy, President Donald Trump later stated that ",["he did not disagree with Vance’s appraisal","https://www.the-sun.com/news/17256408/jd-vance-blames-midterm-elections-loss-iran-war-trump/"]," of the role that frustration with the Iran war played in voters’ minds."]},{"k":"p","s":["But whether this changes Trump’s view on next steps in the ongoing conflict remains unclear. Reporting over the past few weeks has indicated that the U.S. military has been actively preparing options and ",["increasing capabilities in the Persian Gulf region","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/21/us/politics/us-israel-renewed-iran-strikes.html"]," in the event the president directs a resumption of hostilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an ",["expert on Middle East affairs","https://fordschool.umich.edu/faculty/javed-ali"]," and a former senior official at the National Security Council during the first Trump administration, I’m aware that months of conflict have failed to bring Iran to its knees, force regime change or militarily defeat a perceived threat to U.S. assets and allies. Escalating now is unlikely to change those realities – and it carries the additional risk of further damaging Republicans in the eyes of Americans voters as they turn toward the 2028 presidential race."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if Trump were to ratchet up the conflict, moreover, it’s unclear how much wiggle room he’ll have come January facing a Democratic Congress almost ",["uniformly opposed to the war","https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/04/politics/video/jeffries-says-ending-iran-war-will-be-top-of-house-democrats-agenda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sunk costs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of the issue facing Iran war hawks in Washington now is that the conflict has caused serious setbacks for the regime in Tehran without satisfying the officially stated strategic reasons for going to war."]},{"k":"p","s":["They argue that pulling back now – as welcome as that might be for Americans struggling with the associated rising cost of fuel – may allow Iran to rebuild before the conflict is “won.” Moreover, it would render the military and reputational costs already sunk by Washington as wasted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Among the achievements of this war touted by the Trump administration has been the ",["death of former Supreme Leader Ali Khameini","https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/28/middleeast/ayatollah-khamenei-iran-killed-airstrike-intl-latam"],", along with the killing of scores of ",["senior leaders within the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-says-irgc-navy-commander-killed-iranian-top-envoy-said-removed-from-hit-list/"]," – including individuals like the ",["former head of Iran’s National Security Council Ali Larijani","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/3/3/who-is-ali-larijani-the-iranian-official-promising-a-lesson-to-the-us"],". Significant elements of Iran’s air defense and radar network, ",["ballistic missile and drone production, and storage and launch sites","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/16/us-says-it-has-destroyed-iran-missile-capacity-how-is-iran-still-shooting"]," have also been destroyed. And Iran’s ",["already outdated navy and air force","https://www.aerotime.aero/articles/iran-dwindling-air-force-can-jets-still-fly-drone-attacks"]," has been further degraded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the U.S.-imposed ",["naval blockade","https://www.centcom.mil/MEDIA/PUBLIC-RELEASES/Article/4542098/us-forces-to-resume-naval-blockade-against-iran/"]," against Iranian-linked shipping in the Persian Gulf cut off a crucial lifeline for Iran’s economy. And ",["additional sanctions and economic penalties","https://www.state.gov/iran-sanctions/"]," imposed by Washington have served to ",["further devalue Iran’s currency","https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/iran-currency-getting-obliterated-regime-214000456.html"]," and ",["deprive Iran of additional financial links","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/14/how-do-iranians-move-money-abroad-to-avoid-us-sanctions"]," to the international banking system."]},{"k":"h","s":["Down but not out"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet for all the U.S. successes in degrading the Iranian military by limitless aerial bombardment and the significant financial pressure against the Iranian economy, an obvious endgame remains elusive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite weakening the Iranian government – now led by Ali Khameinei’s son, Mojtaba, and a ",["new echelon of senior IRGC commanders","https://www.cnn.com/2026/06/05/middleeast/iran-supreme-leader-adviser-mohsen-rezaei-interview-intl"]," – the Islamic Republic remains intact. Moreover, it ",["still possesses enough ballistic missiles and drones","https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-911221"]," to hold the region at risk, while continuing ",["to impose significant control over its population","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/25/irans-authorities-take-self-sacrifice-mobilisation-campaign-nationwide"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, U.S. military spending continues to rise. In September, the U.S. Congressional Budget Office assessed that the ",["military costs of the Iran War had already totaled US$38 billion","https://www.cbo.gov/publication/62756"],". Since then, that ",["number has only increased","https://www.militarytimes.com/news/2026/10/28/us-costs-of-iran-war-rise-to-over-47-billion-according-to-pentagon-estimate/"],". And that is to say nothing of the associated global economic costs that have resulted from Iran’s de facto closure of the Strait of Hormuz – a key shipping route for oil and gas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Should Trump decide to change course on Iran, he – and others – may think that the money, effort and ",["lives of 19 American servicemen","https://www.militarynews.com/news/national/families-of-some-us-troops-killed-in-the-iran-wars-deadliest-strike-absent-from-white/article_2ddea9b5-b98f-5f10-bd28-3a1b82aa2621.html"]," killed in the conflict would have been spent with no obvious objective achieved. Yet continued military expenditure with no strategic endgame could only magnify those same costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["To Iran, the midterm results have not changed its public position. Mojtaba Khameini has issued statements ",["directing the IRGC to widen the conflict in the region and perhaps beyond","https://www.newsweek.com/khamenei-orders-iran-military-response-without-geographical-limitations-12644735"]," should the U.S. and Israel attack again. At the same time, ",["a statement attributed to him","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-11-04/irans-khamenei-says-us-hostility-will-persist-regardless-of-party-in-power"]," indicates that hostilities between the United States and Iran will persist regardless of the balance of party political power in Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["This raises questions about ",["the prospects for diplomacy","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/31/qatar-iran-us-talks-mediation.html"],". During the summer, the U.S. and Iran agreed to an ",["initial 14-point memorandum of understanding","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/memorandum-of-understanding-between-the-united-states-of-america-and-the-islamic-republic-of-iran/"]," that, if finalized, could have brought a permanent end to the hostilities. But since the ",["60-day clock on that agreement lapsed","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/memorandum-of-understanding-between-the-united-states-of-america-and-the-islamic-republic-of-iran/"],", no parallel diplomatic agreement has emerged."]},{"k":"h","s":["No practical solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even with the major shift in the U.S. political landscape, it remains unclear whether Trump will resume operations against Iran before the new Congress is sworn in. The messy election result in Israel – which has left the ",["pro-war, and potentially outgoing, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyanu","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/netanyahu-reportedly-pressured-israel-military-attack-iran-runup-to-election"]," with potentially more reason to double-down in Iran – only complicates matters."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. military certainly appears to be ready to engage in a new round of attacks against Iran if so directed, and Iran is ready to retaliate. But given ",["the shortcomings in the U.S. inventory","https://nypost.com/2026/09/15/us-news/iran-war-effort-hampered-by-munitions-shortfalls-production-bottlenecks-pentagon-watchdog-finds/"]," – with munitions and missile and air defense capabilities depleted by eight months of war – escalation is something Trump and his inner circle will have to consider with caution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran might force the issue by engaging in ",["asymmetric attacks","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/uk-raf-fairford-terror-plot-iran-2-men-charged-security-offenses/"]," in the region or beyond that they have not attempted already. Or it could launch a coordinated offensive with its partners in the region – notably the Houthis in Yemen, who have become more active ",["in their own conflict with Saudi Arabia","https://time.com/article/2026/10/15/who-are-the-houthi-rebels-saudi-arabia-oil-airport-attacks/"]," in recent months."]},{"k":"p","s":["But save an event that the Trump administration perceives is giving it cover to act, there are no clear indications emerging from Washington as to which way it will move."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vance diagnosed a widely perceived political problem for Republicans: Voters don’t want more war. But what he noticeably didn’t mention was a practical solution. The Middle East conflict – and the United States’ role in it – are, as such, locked in a stalemate."]},{"k":"p","s":["America and Iran have both borne significant political, military and economic costs. A decision not to pursue an endgame would leave those sunk; doing so may only increase them."]}],"chars":6957}};
